---
description: Never expose, read unnecessarily, or commit secrets
alwaysApply: true
---

# Secrets safety

- Never commit `.env`, `.env.local`, or files containing keys/tokens.
- Do not print secrets in chat, logs, commits, or code comments.
- Avoid reading `.env.local` unless strictly required for a task; prefer confirming key *names* only.
- Use `process.env.*` / server-only access; never put service-role or secret keys in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- If a secret may have been exposed, tell the user to rotate it.
